# Exercises Notifications against the compose stack (`make up`): Staff preview the Message templates
# and read the Notifications about an Order, the demo Customer reads their own and saves their
# Notification preferences, and Staff read what the mock SMS and push providers took. Run the token
# requests first; they store tokens for the ones after them.
# A Notification needs a paid Order: check one out in the Storefront as demo@ecomm.local, then set
# @orderId to its ID. Its confirmation is in Mailpit, on http://localhost:8025, a second later. Pick
# and pack its Shipment in the Admin Console, and its ORDER_SHIPPED messages follow; with SMS and
# push on (below), the mock providers take them too. Request a return of a delivered Order's unit in
# the Storefront and set @rmaId to its ID; each step Staff take on it in the Admin Console is
# emailed.

@notifications = http://localhost:8101
@gateway = http://localhost:8000
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token
@orderId = <a paid Order's ID>
@rmaId = <an RMA's ID>
@demoCustomerId = <the demo Customer's ID: the customerId of their Notifications, or their token's sub>

### The demo Customer's token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Staff token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=staff@ecomm.local&password=staff

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Every Message type on every channel, rendered with its sample content, through the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/templates
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### The shipped SMS: a Message type on a channel it goes on
POST {{notifications}}/templates/ORDER_SHIPPED/SMS/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### A channel the Message type doesn't go on: 404
POST {{notifications}}/templates/ORDER_CONFIRMED/SMS/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### One of them; the body's locale is optional, and falls back to en
POST {{notifications}}/templates/ORDER_CONFIRMED/EMAIL/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"locale": "en"}

### A Message type there is none of: 404
POST {{notifications}}/templates/ORDER_EXPLODED/EMAIL/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### The Notifications about the Order, newest first, the address masked: its ORDER_CONFIRMED email, SENT
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/notifications?orderId={{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### The RMA approval, with the Return address and Send-back deadline: an RMA's steps go by email alone
POST {{notifications}}/templates/RMA_APPROVED/EMAIL/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### The Notifications about the RMA, newest first: RMA_REQUESTED, then one per step Staff took
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/notifications?rmaId={{rmaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Staff list by exactly one of orderId, rmaId and customerId: naming none is a 400
GET {{notifications}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### The demo Customer's own Notifications, a page at a time
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/notifications/me?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A Customer can't list by Order: 403
GET {{notifications}}/notifications?orderId={{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### What Mailpit caught: the newest emails first (no token)
GET http://localhost:8025/api/v1/messages?limit=5

### The demo Customer's Notification preferences: email only, until they save theirs
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/preferences/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Turn on SMS, with a mobile number in E.164 form (spaces are dropped), and push
PUT {{gateway}}/api/notifications/preferences/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"phoneNumber": "+49 151 12345678", "sms": true, "push": true}

### A number without its country code: 422 invalidPhoneNumber
PUT {{notifications}}/preferences/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"phoneNumber": "015112345678", "sms": true, "push": false}

### What the mock SMS provider took for the demo Customer, newest first, the number masked
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/mock-providers/sms?customerId={{demoCustomerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### And the mock push provider
GET {{notifications}}/mock-providers/push?customerId={{demoCustomerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Back to email only
PUT {{notifications}}/preferences/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"phoneNumber": null, "sms": false, "push": false}
